<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><documents xmlns:xsi = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation = "HDocumentSchema.xsd"><document type = "H"><pnldref>H1284</pnldref><english><title>Fail to notify the destruction / loss etc of a shotgun outside Great Britain</title><additionalkeywords><additionalkeyword>OUTSIDE</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>ABROAD</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>GREAT BRITAIN</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>35</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>36</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>FIREARMS AMENDMENT ACT 1997</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>DEACTIVATION</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>FAILING</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>FAILED</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>FAILURE</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>DEACTIVATE</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>DEACTIVATED</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>DESTROY</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>DESTROYED</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>LOSE</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>LOST</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>CERTIFICATE</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>CHIEF OFFICER OF POLICE</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>OUTSIDE GREAT BRITAIN</additionalkeyword></additionalkeywords><standardoffencewording>On **(..SPECIFY DATE..) at **(..SPECIFY TOWNSHIP..), being the holder of a certificate relating to a shotgun, namely **(..SPECIFY SHOTGUN..), which had been&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; (A)_[ deactivated]_&lt;br /&gt; (B)_[destroyed]_&lt;br /&gt; (C)_[lost]_&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; outside Great Britain, failed, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 35(3) of the Firearms (Amendment) Act 1997 in that you did not, within fourteen days of that event, give notice of it, by registered post or recorded delivery service or similar from outside the United Kingdom, to the Chief Officer of Police for **(..SPECIFY THE POLICE FORCE..) who had granted your certificate.</standardoffencewording><legislation>Contrary to sections 35(4) and 36(b) of the Firearms (Amendment) Act 1997.</legislation><pointstoprove>date and location&lt;br /&gt; holder of certificate relating to a shotgun&lt;br /&gt; which had been deactivated/destroyed/lost&lt;br /&gt; outside Great Britain&lt;br /&gt; failed without reasonable excuse&lt;br /&gt; to give notice within 14 days of that event&lt;br /&gt; to chief officer of police</pointstoprove><investigatoractions><investigatoraction><code>IA1</code><description>Fingerprint and photograph</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA2</code><description>DNA Samples: If crime scene stain present - take evidential sample If no crime scene stain and DNA not confirmed on PNC - take Criminal Justice sample. If DNA confirmed on PNC - CJ sample not required</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA27</code><description>Confirm proposed charge is appropriately authorised (Police or CPS)</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA28</code><description>Ensure compliance with investigator's obligations re disclosure</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA29</code><description>Consider if case suitable for referral to Financial Investigation Unit and CPS for asset recovery eg confiscation order</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA4</code><description>PNC recordable</description></investigatoraction></investigatoractions><policeandcpschargingresponsibilities>D27968</policeandcpschargingresponsibilities></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></indictmentindicator><structuredindictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></structuredindictmentindicator></indictment><other><powersofarrest>Arrest without warrant</powersofarrest><modeoftrial><code>SIMP</code><description>SUMMARY IMPRISONABLE</description></modeoftrial><timelimitforprosecutions>48 months</timelimitforprosecutions><penalty>Six months imprisonment and / or a fine not exceeding level five on the standard scale.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Time limit for prosecutions:&lt;br /&gt; 48 months&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;On the 12th March 2015 the limit on fines imposed by a Magistrates’ court was removed – as such, the potential fine on summary conviction in relation to an offence committed after this date is unlimited.</penalty><geographicregion><code>GB</code><description>Great Britain</description></geographicregion></other><codes><cjsoffencecode>FA97019</cjsoffencecode><recordableonpncindicator><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></recordableonpncindicator><pncacpooffencecode>11.3.86.1</pncacpooffencecode><notifiabletoho><code>N</code><description>No</description></notifiabletoho><hoclassification>115/97</hoclassification><mopireviewgroup><code>B</code><description>Group 2</description></mopireviewgroup><mopinoteslink>D19586</mopinoteslink><disqualificationclass><code>N</code><description>discretionary disqualification not endorsable</description></disqualificationclass><seatbeltoffence><code>N</code><description>No</description></seatbeltoffence><fptissuedbypolice>0</fptissuedbypolice><fptgraduated>0</fptgraduated><fptgraduatedhigh>0</fptgraduatedhigh><pndissuedbypolice>0</pndissuedbypolice><pndissuedbylocalauthorities>0</pndissuedbylocalauthorities><pndissuedbyothers>0</pndissuedbyothers><roadsidedeposits><code>N</code><description>No</description></roadsidedeposits></codes><libra><cjsoffencecategory><code>CS</code><description>Summary Non-motoring</description></cjsoffencecategory><fineindicator><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></fineindicator><maxfinetypemagct><code>U</code><description>Unlimited</description></maxfinetypemagct><custodialindicator><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></custodialindicator><maxcustodialsentenceunitmagct><code>Months</code><description>Months</description></maxcustodialsentenceunitmagct><maxcustodialsentencelengthmagct>6</maxcustodials